; The light-cone energy of a particle, E - p with E = sqrt(m*m + p*p).  For
; p >> m the two terms cancel, and this is the guarded counterpart to
; examples/gamma-minus-one.fpcore:
;
;   there  1 - sqrt(1-v*v)  is a difference of two positives, so cancellation
;          happens exactly where the value reaches zero -- relative error is
;          genuinely unbounded there and no rewrite helps.  The conjugate's
;          divisor is provably in [1,2], so it fires globally and needs no guard.
;
;   here   sqrt(m*m+p*p) strictly dominates p, so the difference gets small
;          without reaching zero.  But its conjugate divides by
;          sqrt(m*m+p*p) + p, which straddles zero once p may be negative, so
;          the rule cannot fire on the whole box.  The guard p > 0 is what makes
;          it derivable, and only on the arm where the cancellation happens.
(FPCore (m p)
  :name "E - p"
  :pre (and (<= 0.1 m 1) (<= -10 p 10))
  (- (sqrt (+ (* m m) (* p p))) p))
